\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The God of love my shepherd is,
\par And he that doth me feed;
\par While He is mine and I am His,
\par What can I want or need?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He leads me to the tender grass,
\par Where I both feed and rest;
\par Then to the streams that gently pass:
\par In both I have the best.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Or if I stray, He doth convert,
\par And bring my mind in frame,
\par And all this not for my desert,
\par But for His holy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yea, in death's shady black abode
\par Well may I walk, not fear,
\par For Thou art with me, and Thy rod
\par To guide, Thy staff to bear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Surely Thy sweet and wondrous love
\par Shall measure all my days;
\par And, as it never shall remove,
\par So neither shall my praise.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

